[node name="tutorialMarkIngress" parent="." instance=ExtResource("2_k3c6j")]
visible = false
layout_mode = 0
offset_right = 240.0
offset_bottom = 72.0
video_file = "res://graphics/system-map/tutorial/tutorialMarkIngress.ogv"
video_title_text = "Use BARYCENTER VISUALIZER to learn the direction to ping Ingress, and then mark it by using LIDAR to ping it three times."
video_aspect_ratio = 2.0
start_on_video = true
flash_switch_button_until_pressed = true
target_objective_wID = "tutorialMarkIngress"
text_box_size = Vector2(300, 100)
track = NodePath("../../control/scopes_snap_scroll/core_and_value_scroll/core/core_scroll/core_panel/core_margin/core_scroll/barycenter_container")
track_offset = Vector2(0, -355)
background_alpha = 1.0
info = "You did it!

The SYSTEM LIST currently underlines a missing body named Ingress situated further than Prelude. [color=yellow]Our value is maximised by discovering all bodies within a star system[/color]. Let's mark Ingress!

To learn the [i]direction[/i] to ping Ingress, the BARYCENTER VISUALIZER should be used. It displays the [color=yellow]direction[/color] to other bodies [color=yellow]from the locked body[/color] with a [color=yellow]dot[/color]. Dark red dots are beyond the current scan arc.

To ping Ingress, press on 'Prelude' on the SYSTEM LIST to lock, adjust the LIDAR direction so it matches the direction of the orange/yellow dot, and press the 'PING!' button.
[img=150%x75%]res://graphics/objective/tutorial_barycenter_example.png[/img]"

